==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From earlier ''*laugantaki'' (compare dialectal {{m|fi|lauvantaki}}), borrowed from {{bor|fi|non|laugardagr}}. {{cog|et|laupäev}}, {{cog|vot|laukopäive}}, {{cog|izh|laukopäivä}} are from the same origin.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=Fi-lauantai.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{enum|fi|perjantai|sunnuntai|day of the week|la}}
{{fi-noun}}

# [[Saturday]] {{gloss|day of the week; the sixth day of the week in Finland and in the ISO 8601 standard}}

====Usage notes====
As with all days of the week in Finnish, the essive case ({{m|fi||lauantaina}}) is usually used when talking about what will happen or happened on a Saturday.

